{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "9f73b909-d7aa-4298-a4fb-1a3ea26a029f",
    "name": "Abios Case Study — Live API",
    "description": "Spring Boot live-esports API — exercise every public endpoint and probes.\n\n## Before you send requests\n1. Start the app: `bash ./scripts/run.sh` (default **classpath mock**, port **8080**) or Atlas: `bash ./scripts/run-atlas.sh` with `ABIOS_API_KEY`.\n2. Optional full bash sweep (needs curl): `bash ./scripts/run-full-api-verification.sh`.\n\n## Mock vs live\n| Mode | How you know |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Classpath mock** | JSON includes `seriesId` **ser-1001**, player **pl-501**, team **team-1**. No upstream HTTP. |\n| **Atlas** | Different IDs; set collection variable `expectMockData` = `false` so fingerprint tests are skipped. |\n\n## Variables\n- `baseUrl` — e.g. `http://localhost:8080`\n- `expectMockData` — `true` when using default mock; `false` for real Atlas.\n- `testClientIp` — `X-Forwarded-For` hop for an isolated rate-limit bucket (RFC 5737 doc space).\n\n## Sparse fieldsets\nAll three live endpoints support `?fields=f1,f2` to receive only the requested item fields.\nThe `meta` envelope is always returned in full. Unknown field names are silently ignored.\n\n**Player fields:** `playerId`, `nickname`, `firstName`, `lastName`, `role`, `teamId`, `teamName`, `seriesIds`\n**Team fields:** `teamId`, `name`, `abbreviation`, `playerCount`, `seriesIds`\n**Series fields:** `seriesId`, `name`, `gameName`, `state`, `startedAt`, `tier`, `bestOf`, `teamCount`\n\n## API documentation\nSwagger UI: `{{baseUrl}}/swagger-ui` — try every endpoint interactively.\nOpenAPI 3 JSON: `{{baseUrl}}/v3/api-docs`\n\n## Pagination\nAll three live endpoints accept `skip` (0-based offset) and `take` (page size). Omitting both returns the full list.\n\n**Shape:** `{ \"meta\": { fetchedAt, stale, degraded, count, total, skip, take, hasMore }, \"items\": [...] }`. Errors: RFC 7807 where applicable.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Live data",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET /v1/series/live",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status is 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test(\"JSON has meta and items\", () => {",
                  "    const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(j).to.have.property(\"meta\");",
                  "    pm.expect(j).to.have.property(\"items\");",
                  "    pm.expect(j.meta).to.have.property(\"fetchedAt\");",
                  "    pm.expect(j.meta).to.have.property(\"stale\");",
                  "    pm.expect(j.meta).to.have.property(\"degraded\");",
                  "    pm.expect(j.meta).to.have.property(\"count\");",
                  "    pm.expect(j.meta).to.have.property(\"total\");",
                  "    pm.expect(j.meta).to.have.property(\"skip\");",
                  "    pm.expect(j.meta).to.have.property(\"take\");",
                  "    pm.expect(j.meta).to.have.property(\"hasMore\");",
                  "    pm.expect(j.meta.count).to.eql(j.items.length);",
                  "    pm.expect(j.meta.total).to.be.at.least(j.meta.count);",
                  "});",
                  "if (pm.collectionVariables.get(\"expectMockData\") === \"true\") {",
                  "    pm.test(\"Classpath mock fingerprint (series ser-1001)\", () => {",
                  "        const ids = pm.response.json().items.map(i => i.seriesId);",
                  "        pm.expect(ids).to.include(\"ser-1001\");",
                  "    });",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{"key": "Accept", "value": "application/json", "type": "text"}],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/series/live",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["v1", "series", "live"],
              "query": [
                {"key": "skip",         "value": "0",                  "description": "Items to skip (0-based offset). Omit to return all.",         "disabled": true},
                {"key": "take",         "value": "10",                 "description": "Max items to return. Omit or set to 0 to return all.",         "disabled": true},
                {"key": "forceRefresh", "value": "true",               "description": "Bypass cache and fetch fresh data from upstream immediately.", "disabled": true},
                {"key": "fields",       "value": "seriesId,name,state","description": "Comma-separated fields to include per item. Omit for all fields. Available: seriesId, name, gameName, state, startedAt, tier, bestOf, teamCount.", "disabled": true}
              ]
            },
            "description": "All currently live or ongoing esports series. Supports `?skip`/`?take` pagination, `?forceRefresh`, and `?fields=` sparse fieldsets."
          },
          "response": []
        },
